        "abstract": "In this article we report the results obtained from the design and implementation of an analog front-end prototype for Visible Light Communications (VLC). Complementary, a software defined radio device, the USRP (Universal Software Radio Peripheral), is used for producing a BPSK modulated signal. The obtained bit error rate (BER) is 9.76637×10<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">-5</sup> at a bit rate of 2.5 Mbps and a distance of 160 cm between transmitter and receiver. The obtained BER is less than the FEC limit of 3.8×10<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">-3</sup>.",
